From: GloriousEggroll <gloriouseggroll@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] winemidisynth: Add a software synth for MIDI output.

Windows always has a software MIDI synth, and games made with tools like RPG
Maker rely on it. Wine can only send MIDI to a synth the user runs themselves,
so the music in these games is silent otherwise.

Add winemidisynth, which plays MIDI through Wine's FluidSynth with the sound
font named by WINE_MIDI_SOUNDFONT. mmdevapi offers it as device 0 only if the
host has no MIDI device other than Midi Through, so running a synth such as
timidity, or having a hardware device, keeps working as before.

Wine's FluidSynth has the SF2 generator defaults and default modulators turned
off for dmsynth, which sets them itself following DLS. Without them every SF2
voice waits one second before sounding, and short notes never sound at all.
Each module links its own copy of the library, so add wine_fluid_sf2_mode to
turn them back on for winemidisynth only.

https://github.com/GloriousEggroll/proton-ge-custom/issues/949
---
--- a/configure.ac
+++ b/configure.ac
@@ -3435,6 +3435,7 @@
 WINE_CONFIG_MAKEFILE(dlls/winehid.sys)
 WINE_CONFIG_MAKEFILE(dlls/winemac.drv)
 WINE_CONFIG_MAKEFILE(dlls/winemapi)
+WINE_CONFIG_MAKEFILE(dlls/winemidisynth)
 WINE_CONFIG_MAKEFILE(dlls/wineopenxr)
 WINE_CONFIG_MAKEFILE(dlls/wineoss.drv)
 WINE_CONFIG_MAKEFILE(dlls/wineps.drv)
